validated_against: 2026-06-01
---

## 1. TARGET_BOUNDARIES
runtime:
  - TypeScript 5.4 / Next.js 15 App Router

data_stores:
  - Clerk session API (read-only)

authorized_files:
  - src/middleware.ts
  - src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx

forbidden_files:
  - src/db/schema/core.ts
  - .env.production

## 2. INTENT_HAPPY_PATH
1. Unauthenticated user navigates to any protected route.
2. Middleware detects the missing session token.
3. The system redirects the user to /login with a returnUrl query parameter set to the original destination.
4. User authenticates successfully via the Clerk login form.
5. The system redirects the user back to the original destination using the returnUrl parameter.

## 3. EDGE_CRITICAL_UNHAPPY_PATH
1. If the returnUrl parameter contains an external domain or an absolute URL, strip it and redirect to the dashboard root instead. Do not redirect to external sites.
2. If the Clerk session check throws a network error, redirect to /login without a returnUrl. Do not display a 500 error page.
3. If the user lands on /login while already authenticated, redirect immediately to the dashboard root. Do not render the login form.

## 4. REGRESSION_FENCE
- No dependencies declared. No preservation rules required.

## 5. CONTEXT_DEBT_NOTE
The returnUrl stripping rule (unhappy path 1) was added after a security review on 2026-03-14. The decision was to strip silently rather than show an error, because the UX team found error messages on redirect caused user confusion. Do not change this behaviour without a new security review.
